Interpretation
==============================================================================
The anti-causal fraction is SUBSTANTIAL (order 10-50%) for z=O(1) (the
'boundary layer' regime, matching the archive's own established
terminology, h1_u2_boundary_layer_attempt) and DECREASES as z grows, but
does not vanish at any FIXED, finite z tested (still >0 even at z=100,
just numerically small there). This confirms quantitatively -- not just
qualitatively -- that Psi(x,y)'s dependence on Phi genuinely reaches
points with LARGER z than the current one, at every finite z, with the
leakage concentrated (but not confined) to the boundary-layer regime
where prior fronts (waves 20-31) already found the hardest open content
of this whole sub-lineage (H1's own uniform-in-x rate, DISC-DEC-127).

